# Editor-tooling cache (a hook.cache.json per directory), created wherever a
# file gets touched — six had accumulated across apps/ and packages/ before
# anyone noticed. No leading slash, so this matches at any depth.
.impeccable/

# Claude Code's project-scoped MCP servers. Personal authoring tooling, not
# project config: the one that appeared here declares shadcn's MCP server, and
# shadcn is not a dependency of this workspace — there is no `components.json`
# and no `shadcn` in any package.json. `apps/web` follows shadcn/ui's PATTERN
# (a hand-written `cn`, cva variant maps) and its own comments say so, which is
# a reference, not a toolchain.
#
# Committing it would put an unpinned `npx shadcn@latest mcp` in front of every
# teammate, for a tool the build never invokes. Genuinely shared agent tooling
# still belongs in the repo — `.claude/skills/running-perfportal-locally` is
# committed precisely because it is.
.mcp.json

# On-prem runner and ingest working state. `RUNNER_ARTIFACT_DIR`,
# `RUNNER_WORK_DIR` and `RUNNER_LOG_DIR` all default to a path under
# `.perfportal/`, and that default is RELATIVE — so each process resolves it
# against its own working directory. Run the API and the runner the way this
# repo's own docs do (`pnpm --filter …`, which starts each app in its own
# package directory) and you get `apps/api/.perfportal/` and
# `apps/runner/.perfportal/` as separate trees inside the checkout.
#
# It is uploaded jars, extracted bundles and per-job logs: megabytes on the
# first on-prem run, unbounded after that, and none of it reproducible or
# shared. No leading slash, so this matches wherever a process happens to
# start.
#
# (The same relative default is why an artifact uploaded through the API is
# invisible to a runner started from a different directory — point both at one
# absolute path, or give them a shared volume, as `infra/` does.)
.perfportal/
